/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  MEASURED-AND-CORRELATED vapour-liquid equilibrium of propene (1) + propane (2)
  at 100 degF = 310.9278 K.

  SOURCE (the page, not an archive): Laurance, D.R.; Swift, G.W.  "Relative
  Volatility of Propane-Propene System from 100-160 F", J. Chem. Eng. Data 17
  (1972) 333-336, Table IV "Results of Calculations" (p. 335), the block
  T = 100 F.  Read from the page image, every digit.  x is the LIQUID mole
  fraction of PROPENE (the paper's Figure 2 axis).  The paper's own words on
  what the numbers are: the vapour pressures of Table I were MEASURED (probable
  error 0.1 %) and correlated (Antoine for the pure fluids, Manley's
  deviation-from-Raoult form for the mixtures, Tables II and III); Table IV then
  COMPUTES y, the bubble pressure P, the liquid volume VL, the vapour
  compressibility Z and the relative volatility alpha by integrating the
  isothermal general coexistence equation.  No vapour composition was sampled
  (the method needs none).  So y and alpha here are DERIVED FROM MEASURED
  PRESSURES, with the paper's stated error of +-0.005 in alpha; P is the
  correlation of the measured pressures.  Pressure in psia.

  Columns are the props bench's overlay names: x[propylene], P_bubble,
  y_eqT_propylene; `alpha` is the paper's column alpha = (y1/x1)/(y2/x2), kept
  for the gate (bin/curate/check_olefin_vle.py), which recomputes it from the
  engine's y and compares.  The pure ends (x = 0 and 1) are not listed: there
  y = x and alpha is a limit.
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

property     binaryVLE.P_bubble;
system       ( propylene propane );
temperature  310.9278 K;

provenance
{
    source       measured;
    reviewStatus transcribedNotCheckedAgainstArticle;
    citation     "Laurance, D.R.; Swift, G.W. (1972). Relative volatility of propane-propene system from 100-160 F. J. Chem. Eng. Data 17, 333-336, Table IV (p. 335). doi:10.1021/je60054a011";
    sourceFile   "laurance1972-propane-propene-relative-volatility.pdf";
    sha256       "604276ffa5904a88de50eb252f48c98117ec25fe4d7cbfff0e853299d222056b";   // of that PDF
}

columns
(
    { name x[propylene];  unit -;  }
    { name P_bubble;  unit psi;  }
    { name y_eqT_propylene;  unit -;  }
    { name alpha;  unit -;  }
);

data
(
    0.1000  194.01  0.1178  1.2022
    0.2000  199.06  0.2286  1.1855
    0.3000  203.70  0.3338  1.1692
    0.4000  207.97  0.4347  1.1536
    0.5000  211.90  0.5325  1.1390
    0.6000  215.50  0.6281  1.1257
    0.7000  218.84  0.7222  1.1143
    0.8000  221.94  0.8155  1.1048
    0.9000  224.85  0.9081  1.0976
);
